 center immediately. The move **e7-e5** is the most principled response because it:\n- Occupies the center with a pawn\n- Opens diagonals for both the dark-squared bishop and queen\n- Prepares for natural development (Nf6, Bc5/e7, 0-0)\n- Follows the classical opening principle: "Control the center early"\n\nThis move gives Black an immediate advantage in the opening as White has already used a tempo on a flank pawn move.\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5'}
