ut doesn't address the immediate threat of the queen.\n\nThe most forcing and best move appears to be **N: g8-f6**, which:\n- Develops a piece with tempo\n- Attacks White's misplaced queen\n- Prepares kingside castling\n- Controls central squares\n- Follows sound opening principles (develop pieces, control center)\n\nReason: Developing the knight to f6 attacks White's queen on h4, forcing it to retreat while I gain time and development. This is a classical principle: when your opponent places pieces aggressively early, develop with threats. The knight on f6 also controls important central squares and prepares castling kingside after developing the f8 bishop.\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
