8-c5** - Develops the bishop to an active diagonal pointing at f2, another weak point near White's king.\n\nReason: I choose **N: f6-g4** because it creates an immediate double threat: attacking f2 (which is only defended by the king) and potentially coordinating with my queen on h4 for a devastating attack. The knight on g4 cannot be easily driven away, and it forces White to deal with serious tactical problems. With White's king still in the center and undeveloped pieces, this aggressive knight move maximizes pressure and winning chances.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-g4"}
