ill require immediate attention from White. The pawn attacks c2 and controls key squares. White will be forced into a defensive posture to stop the pawn, giving me time to develop my other pieces and coordinate an attack. This is a concrete, forcing move that leverages my best asset in the position.\n\nAnswer: P: d4-d3"}
