for White - the pawn will be one square from promotion and very difficult to stop. White's pieces are not well-coordinated to deal with this threat. The rook on a2 cannot easily reach c2, and White would be forced into desperate measures. This move maintains maximum pressure and gives me the best winning chances by forcing White into a defensive, reactionary position.\n\nAnswer: P: d3-c2"}
