e:\n- It addresses my most critical weakness: my exposed king in the center\n- It connects my rooks and activates the h8 rook\n- White's pieces are positioned to potentially exploit my uncastled king\n- After securing king safety, I can pursue aggressive plans with my active bishop and develop my remaining pieces\n- This is a fundamental chess principle: secure the king before launching attacks\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
