rcing move puts White on the defensive and the King has very limited escape squares (likely only h4 or h2). This check allows me to seize the initiative and potentially coordinate my pieces for a mating attack. With my two rooks, bishop, and knight all active, forcing White's king to move to an even more exposed square could lead to a quick victory.\n\nAnswer: N: h2-g4"}
