o respond immediately. This Knight move also centralizes my Knight on an excellent square where it controls key squares (c5, d6, f6, g5, g3, f2, d2, c3). Given that White's King is exposed and I have material advantage with two Rooks, forcing White's King to move will allow me to consolidate my position and potentially launch a decisive attack.\n\nAnswer: N: d2-e4"}
