\n1 |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a6, R: a8-b8, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, P: c6-c5, B: c8-d7, R: e8-d8, R: e8-e7, R: e8-f8, P: g7-g5, P: g7-g6, K: g8-f7, K: g8-f8, K: g8-h8, P: h7-h5, P: h7-h6]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I'm playing as Black. White has a very advanced position with their King on e5 and Rook on e4, both deep in Black's territory. White has only two pawns left (a5, b4) while Black has more pieces intact (2 Rooks, 1 Bishop, 1 Knight, 5 Pawns). However, White's pieces are dangerously active. My King on g8 appears relatively safe but constrained. The Black Rook on e8 is on the same file as White's King and Rook, creating tactical possibilities.\n\nEvaluation: \n1. **R: e8-e7** - Attacks the White King on e5, forcing it to move. This gives check and disrupts White's coordination.\n2. **R: e8-d8** - Moves the Rook to safety on the d-file, but passive and doesn't challenge White's advanced pieces.\n3. **K: g8-f8** - Moves King toward the center/Rook, but doesn't address the immediate threat of White's advanced pieces.\n4. **P: c6-c5** - Advances a central pawn but doesn't create immediate threats.\n5. **B: c8-d7** - Develops the Bishop but blocks the d-file and doesn't create immediate pressure.\n\nThe key insight is that White's King on e5 is exposed. By playing R: e8-e7, I give check and force the White King to retreat, after which I can potentially coordinate my pieces better.\n\nReason: R: e8-e7 is the strongest move because:\n- It gives check to the exposed White King on e5\n- Forces White's King to retreat, reducing their attacking potential\n- Activates my Rook to the 7th rank (a powerful square)\n- Maintains initiative and puts White on the defensive\n- After the King moves, I can better coordinate my superior material\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e7"}
